          "body": "Fixes #3\n\n## Problem\n\nCare FE exposes the auth context to plugs as `window.AuthUserContext` (see [care_fe `src/index.tsx`](https://github.com/ohcnetwork/care_fe/blob/develop/src/index.tsx) and `docs/care-apps-architecture-note.md`), but the template's `declare global { interface Window { … } }` only declares `CARE_API_URL`. A freshly scaffolded plug that uses the host context does not type-check.\n\nReproduction (scaffold from this repo's `src/init.js`, `npm install`, add a hook that reads `window.AuthUserContext`):\n\n```\n$ npx tsc --noEmit -p tsconfig.app.json\nsrc/hooks/useAuthUser.ts(4,33): error TS2339: Property 'AuthUserContext' does not exist on type 'Window & typeof globalThis'.\nsrc/hooks/useAuthUser.ts(5,13): error TS2339: Property 'user' does not exist on type '{}'.\n```\n\n## Fix\n\n- `template/src/index.tsx`: add `AuthUserContext: Context<AuthContextType | null>` to the `Window` augmentation (same type the host assigns).\n- `template/src/lib/types/common.ts`: add an `AuthContextType` mirroring the commonly used members of care_fe's `AuthContextType` (`user`, `isAuthenticating`, `isVerifyingMFA`, `signOut`), typed with the template's existing `UserBase`. Plugs that need more of the host context can extend it.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Scaffolded a plug from this branch, `npm install`, added `src/hooks/useAuthUser.ts` using `useContext(window.AuthUserContext)`:\n  - before: `tsc --noEmit -p tsconfig.app.json` → 3× TS2339 (above)\n  - after: `tsc --noEmit -p tsconfig.app.json` → exit 0; `vite build` succeeds\n- `prettier --check` and `eslint` pass on the changed template files (using the template's own config).\n- `npm pack` → tarball's `template/src/index.tsx` contains the new declaration.\n",
